# Secrets, wherever they end up. android/.gitignore and the bots' own .gitignore files cover
# their folders; these catch a key saved anywhere else in the repository by mistake.
*.keystore
*.jks
keystore.properties
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
.env
.env.local
.vercel/

# release/<version>/ holds what flutter/build-apk.ps1 builds (the APK, the AAB, their mapping and
# symbols), committed, except any file over 100 MB, GitHub's limit, which it lists at the end of
# this file to go only on the GitHub release.

# The 1.0.x Capacitor app, retired in 1.1.0 for flutter/: what's left of it on disk (its key,
# google-services.json, node_modules, builds) stays out of git.
/android/
